WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.568
[music playing]

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:04.871
Spear fishing in Hawaii.

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:07.874
I'm like a fish out of water.

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:11.444
Thank god, I've got free
diving champ Kimi for a guide.

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:12.912
She makes it look so easy.

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:17.317
[music playing]

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:18.852
Damn, she's good.

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:24.824
Despite my fetching camouflage,
I can't hear a thing.

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:28.862
You were that close!

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:29.696
[inaudible]

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:30.630
That close.

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:31.631
Don't get frustrated.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:32.866
Oh, man.

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:33.767
KIMI WERNER: Like really.

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:34.834
You were almost there.

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.302
That was a good fish, too.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:40.340
How do you keep your
breath under such control?

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:43.243
Because you're holding
on to the seabed.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:45.145
You have the spear in the other.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:47.814
KIMI WERNER: And the
current is pushing you

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:48.882
back and forth the entire time.

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:49.749
GORDON RAMSAY: Yeah.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:50.784
[inaudible]

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.018
KIMI WERNER: It's a lot of work.

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:53.253
GORDON RAMSAY: Right.
Here we go.

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:54.621
KIMI WERNER: That
was awesome, though.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.489
[music playing]

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:04.030
Right.

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:06.833
Hold my breath.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:10.136
Line up my sights.

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:12.338
This is just like shooting
fish in a barrel--

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:16.509
a very big
Pacific-Ocean-sized barrel.

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:17.310
Bingo.

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.486
[music playing]

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:30.490
Whoo, Whoo, Whoo, Whoo!

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:31.624
Awesome!

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:32.826
GORDON RAMSAY: A beauty.

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:34.494
I held onto the rock,
[inaudible] down the cord.

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:37.063
I just waited for him to pop up.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.698
Oh, that was awesome.

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:39.466
GORDON RAMSAY: Whoo.

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:40.500
I don't want to come out.

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:41.134
I know.

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:42.068
Amazing.

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:43.670
Honestly.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:44.704
What a teacher.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:46.339
It makes you want
to live under water.

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:47.874
It's that exciting.

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:49.108
You don't want to come up.

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:50.310
I want to go back again.

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:51.244
This is an nenue.

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:52.078
GORDON RAMSAY: An nenue?

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:53.580
Yes.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.081
GORDON RAMSAY: Did you grow
up eating fish like this?

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:56.583
KIMI WERNER: My dad
would go spear fishing

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:58.885
to put food on the table and
this is one of the main fish

00:01:58.952 --> 00:01:59.719
that he fed us.
- Wow.

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:00.520
How cool.

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:01.354
Beautiful.

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:02.689
So you literally eat this raw?

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.591
KIMI WERNER: We always
would eat this fish raw.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:08.161
This fish eats a lot of seaweed,
and so it tastes different

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:09.629
all on different
parts of the island

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:12.165
depending on what type of
seaweed is growing there.

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:13.333
Thank you.

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:14.367
Wow.

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:15.902
KIMI WERNER: Can you taste that?

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:17.270
That's delicious.

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:18.838
And it does taste a little
bit seaweedy, salty.

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:20.907
KIMI WERNER: A lot of times
we add seaweed for flavor.

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:22.408
GORDON RAMSAY: Yeah.

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:23.676
KIMI WERNER: With this fish,
it's already preseasoned--

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:24.644
GORDON RAMSAY: Thank you.

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:25.612
KIMI WERNER:
--because of its diet.

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:27.680
[music playing]

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:29.449
GORDON RAMSAY: I mean, it
was like the perfect trip

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:32.719
to any fishmonger you'll
ever go to your entire life.

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:34.487
I didn't think it would
taste that good and my god,

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:38.224
without any dressing,
without any chili or any soy,

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:39.692
and so that's got
me thinking now.

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:43.096
You know, do I make this
feast normally around the fish

00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:45.231
locally or is it meats?

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:48.668
Right now, honestly,
I'm spoiled for choice.

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:50.603
[music playing]

